## Why This Is Asked

This question probes on-device real-time hazard detection and 3D distance estimation under unseen categories, reflecting safety-critical constraints common in field deployments.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time monocular depth on edge
- On-device meta-learning (5-shot)
- Synthetic+real data with domain randomization
- Temporal tracking and occlusion robustness
- Evaluation: detection, depth error, latency

## Code Example

```javascript
function forward(img, backbone, detectorHead, depthHead) {
  const feats = backbone.extract(img);
  const boxes = detectorHead.predict(feats);
  const depth = depthHead.predict(feats);
  return { boxes, depth };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you ablate depth head accuracy vs. detector latency?
- What failure modes dominate in cluttered sites, and how would you mitigate them?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests solving interdependent CV tasks under tight latency with on-device adaptation for unseen objects, in realistic cluttered scenes.

## Key Concepts
- Shared backbone with multi-head decoders
- Joint losses: depth, normals, affordance, temporal consistency
- 5-shot on-device adaptation for novel objects
- Edge-GPU constraints (<25 ms) and robustness to occlusion/dynamic lighting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-architecture wiring
function forward(x) {
  const z = encoder(x);
  const d = depthHead(z);
  const n = normalsHead(z);
  const a = affordanceHead(z);
  return { depth: d, normals: n, affordances: a };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you diagnose a failing grasp affordance map with occlusion?
- What ablations would you run to validate the importance of temporal consistency?

